  "answer": {
    "response": "Impact chain: caller → `EmailProducer.enqueue` → BullMQ queue `email` / job `send-email` → `EmailProcessor.process` → `MailDeliveryService.send`.\n\n- Payload contract: `SendEmailJob` currently contains `recipient`, the `template` union, and `variables` in `src/notifications/jobs/email.job.ts:1`. `locale` belongs in this shared interface. The fixture contains no locale definition, so its exact type or allowed values cannot be determined from repository evidence.\n- Producer: `EmailProducer.enqueue` accepts `SendEmailJob` and passes the payload unchanged to `emailQueue.add(\"send-email\", payload)` in `src/notifications/email.producer.ts:8`. A required locale will therefore be enforced at typed call sites automatically. No producer callers exist inside this fixture.\n- Consumer: `EmailProcessor` consumes `Job<SendEmailJob>` from the `email` queue and forwards `job.data` unchanged to `MailDeliveryService.send` in `src/notifications/email.processor.ts:7`. The delivery service also accepts `SendEmailJob`, but currently reads only `template` and `recipient`; adding locale to the contract alone will not create localized behavior (`src/notifications/mail-delivery.service.ts:6`).\n- Tests: the only existing affected test is `test/notifications/email.processor.test.ts:5`. Its job fixture omits locale and should be updated to include it so the existing whole-payload assertion verifies forwarding. Because the fixture is cast with `job as never`, adding a required interface field may not make this test fail at compile time. There are no producer or delivery-service tests; those would be needed to verify queue serialization or locale-dependent delivery behavior respectively.\n\nThis was a read-only impact analysis; no files were changed or tests run.",
